WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.233 align:middle line:90%


00:00:00.233 --> 00:00:03.203 align:middle line:84%
We just showed that because of
the intrinsic incompleteness

00:00:03.203 --> 00:00:05.705 align:middle line:84%
of models eliminating
bias in all dimensions

00:00:05.705 --> 00:00:07.741 align:middle line:90%
is mathematically impossible.

00:00:07.741 --> 00:00:10.643 align:middle line:84%
We could no doubt decrease
bias among some groups

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:14.080 align:middle line:84%
to a certain degree, with an
acceptably small but still

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.149 align:middle line:90%
significant margin of error.

00:00:16.149 --> 00:00:19.052 align:middle line:84%
Even if we got rid of bias in
some predefined dimensions,

00:00:19.052 --> 00:00:21.354 align:middle line:84%
we would still have it
in other dimensions.

00:00:21.354 --> 00:00:23.423 align:middle line:90%
But that's precisely it.

00:00:23.423 --> 00:00:26.393 align:middle line:84%
We want equality in at
least some dimensions,

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:27.594 align:middle line:90%
the important ones.

00:00:27.594 --> 00:00:28.461 align:middle line:90%
That is good.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:31.297 align:middle line:84%
How do you choose which
dimensions are important?

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:31.965 align:middle line:90%
Alvis.

00:00:31.965 --> 00:00:34.267 align:middle line:84%
One important
dimension is wealth.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.902 align:middle line:90%
Good.

00:00:35.902 --> 00:00:39.039 align:middle line:84%
So even you five, the
top engineering students

00:00:39.039 --> 00:00:41.875 align:middle line:84%
in your class at the top
engineering school, should get

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:45.678 align:middle line:84%
paid just as much as someone
like Dean, the paper collector.

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:50.884 align:middle line:84%
Well, he is a very nice
fellow, if a bit strange.

00:00:50.884 --> 00:00:55.088 align:middle line:84%
But no, we think we should be
rewarded for the contributions

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:57.057 align:middle line:90%
that we make to society.

00:00:57.057 --> 00:01:00.193 align:middle line:84%
But wealth should be
distributed more equally.

00:01:00.193 --> 00:01:00.727 align:middle line:90%
That's right.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.662 align:middle line:84%
But how do you decide
how equal it should be?

00:01:02.662 --> 00:01:05.832 align:middle line:90%


00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.767 align:middle line:84%
Perhaps the problem
is once again

00:01:07.767 --> 00:01:10.904 align:middle line:84%
that mathematics in its
homogenization of kinds

00:01:10.904 --> 00:01:13.640 align:middle line:84%
is not the right way
to address the problem.

00:01:13.640 --> 00:01:15.175 align:middle line:90%
Let me ask you this--

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:18.445 align:middle line:84%
is it really equality that
you want, or is it justice?

00:01:18.445 --> 00:01:19.312 align:middle line:90%
Justice.

00:01:19.312 --> 00:01:19.979 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:01:19.979 --> 00:01:21.781 align:middle line:90%
I'll go with justice.

00:01:21.781 --> 00:01:25.118 align:middle line:84%
Great that you two
agree on something.

00:01:25.118 --> 00:01:26.252 align:middle line:90%
Glenda.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:29.122 align:middle line:84%
They should go hand in
hand, justice and equality.

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:29.689 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:01:29.689 --> 00:01:31.524 align:middle line:90%
Isn't equality justice?

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.827 align:middle line:84%
I think we need to add
another consideration,

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:36.096 align:middle line:84%
since we are beginning to
delve into the complex human

00:01:36.096 --> 00:01:38.131 align:middle line:84%
questions underlying
our definition

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:40.233 align:middle line:90%
and perception of bias.

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:41.401 align:middle line:90%
So let me ask you this.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:44.304 align:middle line:84%
Which is most important--
equality, justice,

00:01:44.304 --> 00:01:46.906 align:middle line:90%
or happiness?

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.074 align:middle line:90%
Sophie.

00:01:48.074 --> 00:01:50.243 align:middle line:90%
I would say happiness.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:51.978 align:middle line:84%
Even if someone has
more than you do,

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.913 align:middle line:84%
and even if they
don't deserve it,

00:01:53.913 --> 00:01:57.083 align:middle line:84%
it doesn't matter to you
as long as you are happy.

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:59.819 align:middle line:84%
Think of all the people
born into rich families.

00:01:59.819 --> 00:02:01.654 align:middle line:84%
They're typically
not happy since they

00:02:01.654 --> 00:02:04.858 align:middle line:84%
don't need to have a goal, and
therefore they don't have one.

00:02:04.858 --> 00:02:07.760 align:middle line:84%
I would still have a goal if I
were born into a rich family.

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.162 align:middle line:84%
Why do they need
a goal if they're

00:02:09.162 --> 00:02:10.797 align:middle line:90%
having such a good time?

00:02:10.797 --> 00:02:13.933 align:middle line:84%
Because people need to
have a purpose to be happy.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:17.804 align:middle line:84%
And how can people be happy
if they're not treated fairly?

00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:21.074 align:middle line:84%
So we have equality,
justice, and happiness,

00:02:21.074 --> 00:02:24.210 align:middle line:84%
but it is unclear which
is most important.

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.145 align:middle line:90%
Glenda.

00:02:25.145 --> 00:02:27.147 align:middle line:84%
Can't they be of
equal importance?

00:02:27.147 --> 00:02:28.381 align:middle line:90%
Actually, no.

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.049 align:middle line:90%
They are certainly interrelated.

00:02:30.049 --> 00:02:33.119 align:middle line:84%
But since they are at
least somewhat different

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:35.555 align:middle line:84%
and since, as we saw, they
can conflict, one of them

00:02:35.555 --> 00:02:39.192 align:middle line:84%
has to be most important, has to
take precedence over the other.

00:02:39.192 --> 00:02:42.128 align:middle line:84%
I think that justice is more
important than equality.

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:45.398 align:middle line:84%
After all, we don't want
everyone to be the exact same,

00:02:45.398 --> 00:02:49.502 align:middle line:84%
but still justice and
equality are related.

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:52.772 align:middle line:84%
People can be unequal because
they're treated unfairly.

00:02:52.772 --> 00:02:55.875 align:middle line:84%
They can also be unequal
due to luck, good or bad.

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:58.311 align:middle line:84%
I don't think that happiness
can be the standard.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:01.414 align:middle line:84%
We need equality, and that's
why mathematics is still

00:03:01.414 --> 00:03:04.350 align:middle line:84%
so important, because we
can employ it rigorously

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.052 align:middle line:90%
to make everyone equal.

00:03:06.052 --> 00:03:09.889 align:middle line:84%
But if everyone is the same,
wouldn't the world be drab?

00:03:09.889 --> 00:03:11.891 align:middle line:84%
I mean, what if all
of us were the same?

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:14.894 align:middle line:84%
We wouldn't even be able to
have this dialogue, as we'd all

00:03:14.894 --> 00:03:16.529 align:middle line:90%
be making the same point.

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.997 align:middle line:84%
There would be
nothing interesting,

00:03:17.997 --> 00:03:21.834 align:middle line:84%
as everyone is reduced
to a forced homogeneity.

00:03:21.834 --> 00:03:23.670 align:middle line:84%
Besides, how do
you make everyone

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.872 align:middle line:84%
equal without
violating their rights?

00:03:25.872 --> 00:03:28.241 align:middle line:84%
We're going to have to
violate some rights to make

00:03:28.241 --> 00:03:30.009 align:middle line:90%
people at least more equal.

00:03:30.009 --> 00:03:33.813 align:middle line:84%
But then maybe I guess
that's not justice.

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:34.447 align:middle line:90%
Yeah.

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:37.684 align:middle line:84%
Isn't it the essence of tyranny
when rights are violated

00:03:37.684 --> 00:03:39.352 align:middle line:90%
in the name of justice?

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.220 align:middle line:90%
Yes.

00:03:40.220 --> 00:03:42.589 align:middle line:84%
We have strong reasons
not to want that.

00:03:42.589 --> 00:03:44.557 align:middle line:84%
We want equality,
but we certainly

00:03:44.557 --> 00:03:47.827 align:middle line:84%
don't want to violate
people's rights to get it.

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:50.263 align:middle line:90%
But what do we do?

00:03:50.263 --> 00:03:52.298 align:middle line:90%
Here we are at an impasse again.

00:03:52.298 --> 00:03:53.933 align:middle line:84%
How do we understand
this conflict

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:56.970 align:middle line:90%
between equality and rights?

00:03:56.970 --> 00:03:59.204 align:middle line:84%
By the way, professor,
what about that other way

00:03:59.204 --> 00:04:00.139 align:middle line:90%
that you promised?